{"d":20,"passage":{"title":"国富论","author":"Adam Smith","text":"Bar or ingot gold is received in proportion to its fineness, compared with the above foreign gold coin. In general, however, something more is given upon coin of a known fineness, than upon gold and silver bars, of which the fineness cannot be ascertained but by a process of melting and assaying. The proportions between the bank price, the mint price, and the market price of gold bullion, are nearly the same. A person can generally sell his receipt for the difference between the mint price of bullion and the market price. The receipt and the bank credit seldom keep long together, and there is no occasion that they should. The owners of bank credits, and the holders of receipts, constitute two different sorts of creditors against the bank. The holder of a receipt cannot draw out the bullion for which it is granted, without re-assigning to the bank a sum of bank money equal to the price at which the bullion had been received."},"words":[{"w":"synthesis","uk":"'sinθisis","us":"/'sinθisis/","p":"v.","m":"=synthesize 合成；综合","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":{"t":"But Plato erroneously imagines that the synthesis is separable from the analysis, and that the method of science can anticipate science.","w":"理想国","a":"Plato (B. Jowett trans.)"},"b":null},{"w":"fiber","uk":"'faibə","us":"/'faibə/","p":"n.","m":"=fibre 纤维；纤维素","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"medline","uk":"'med,lain","us":"/'med,lain/","p":"","m":"n. <美>联机医学文献分析和检索系统","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"innovative","uk":"'inəjveitiv","us":"/'inəjveitiv/","p":"adj.","m":"a. 革新的, 创新的, 富有革新精神的","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"massage","uk":"'mæsɑːʒ","us":"/'mæsɑʒ/","p":"","m":"n. 按摩, 揉 vt. 按摩, 揉","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"tampa","uk":"'tæmpə","us":"/'tæmpə/","p":"","m":"n. 坦帕市（美国佛罗里达州西部港市）","f":[],"c":[],"o":null,"q":null,"b":null},{"w":"python","uk":"'paiθɒn","us":"/'paiθɑn/","p":"","m":"n. 大蟒